  "claims": [
    "Outlook.com is rejecting email from domains without DMARC records.",
    "Since November 5, 2026, Microsoft's consumer mail service has been turning away some email from domains that don't publish a DMARC record.",
    "This affects mail sent to outlook.com, hotmail.com, live.com, or msn.com addresses.",
    "The change was unannounced.",
    "DMARC helps prevent spoofing, phishing, and business email compromise.",
    "A domain that authenticates is much harder to impersonate.",
    "The fix is one DNS record.",
    "DMARC passes only when SPF or DKIM passes for the domain in your From address.",
    "DMARC at p=none is now the baseline for major mailbox providers."
